From 4ab9a8d5b0176f5aef858ef45960e51f1377257a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vuln Patch Pipeline <vuln-patch@chainguard.dev>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 12:15:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Close Webserver.doReply streams and reject malformed request
 lines

javassist.tools.web.Webserver.doReply read the request path with
cmd.substring(5, cmd.indexOf(' ', 5)). A "GET /" request line with no
space after the path made indexOf return -1, so substring threw an
unchecked StringIndexOutOfBoundsException that skipped the socket
cleanup (CWE-20, CWE-755). The file and class-file branches also opened
a FileInputStream and closed it only after the whole response was
written, so a client that disconnected mid-transfer left the stream
open (CWE-404, CWE-772). Repeated requests could exhaust file
descriptors.

A request line with no space after the path is now refused with the
existing BadHttpRequest (400 Bad Request). Both file-serving branches
read and write inside try/finally and always close the input stream,
including when the client disconnects. Well-formed requests are served
as before.

Adds WebserverResourceLeakExploitTest.

Cgp-Finding: CGP-9x7f-cpwh-f59q
